 """
+# RANKING. `score` is the sector percentile and compute_gauge_scores.py (stage 4) writes it, not
+# this stage, so a gauge recomputed on refreshed statements used to land beside the ranking of
+# its PREVIOUS value - a correct number under a stale rank, with nothing to show it. A percentile
+# only means anything for the value it ranked, so a changed value clears it and it stays absent
+# until stages 3 and 4 have BOTH run again. `score` is added by stage 4 (ALTER TABLE), so a fresh
+# database has not got the column and the plain upsert is used instead.
+SQL_UPSERT_CLEARING_SCORE = SQL_UPSERT.rstrip() + """,
+    score=CASE WHEN excluded.value IS value THEN score ELSE NULL END
